# Favicon: Cream-background crimson T

The site favicon is the **centered crimson serif T on a cream background**. High-quality master: `server/scripts/favicon-locked/source.png` (1024×1024, lossless). Never the cream/orange corner-triangle UI motif.

## Locked known-good (do not drift)

Known-good copies live in `server/scripts/favicon-locked/`. Spec: `LOCKED.json`. **Never overwrite `source.png`.**

**Tab actually uses PNGs, not the SVG.** HTML does not link `favicon.svg`. Chrome typically shows `favicon-16.png` at 1x and `favicon-32.png` at 2x. Google Search uses `favicon-48.png`. `/favicon.ico` is served from `favicon-48.png`. Cache buster: `FAVICON_VERSION` in `server/utils/seo.js` (currently `'15'`).

Do not regenerate this icon as a Georgia text draw. Tab sizes are scaled from the 1024 master.

## Never change without explicit user request

Do **not** edit, regenerate, reorder, or replace any file in `public/favicon*`, `public/apple-touch-icon.png`, `server/scripts/favicon-locked/`, or `views/partials/seo-head.ejs` favicon links unless the user explicitly asks.

## Testing a new icon

1. Leave `server/scripts/favicon-locked/` untouched (especially `source.png`).
2. Swap only the public files to test.
3. If it is not good, restore instantly:

```bash
npm run restore:favicon
```

## Forbidden icon

The corner-triangle motif (cream `#EFE8DC` + orange `#C16A28` wedge) must never appear in favicon assets. It is a **navigation UI element**, not the tab icon.

## Required assets

- `server/scripts/favicon-locked/source.png` — 1024×1024 master
- `public/favicon-16.png`, `favicon-32.png`, `favicon-48.png`
- `public/apple-touch-icon.png`
- `/favicon.ico` is served by Express as a copy of `favicon-48.png` (no separate .ico file)

## If favicons must be regenerated

Run:

```bash
npm run generate:favicon
```

Then confirm:

```bash
npm run verify:favicon
```

If the result is wrong, restore instead of hand-fixing:

```bash
npm run restore:favicon
```

## New pages

All pages must include favicons only through `views/partials/seo-head.ejs` (which includes `favicon-links.ejs`). Do not add separate favicon links unless updating those partials for the whole site.

**Do not link `favicon.svg` in HTML.** Tab icons must use the PNG/ICO assets only.
